The backbones reproduce each notebook's training flow and configuration values;
several blocks reproduce its data preparation, chat template and reward
functions. That makes them derivative works, and LGPL-3.0 does not permit adding
restrictions such as a noncommercial clause to a work derived from it.

**So these files are under LGPL-3.0**, and you may use them commercially on
LGPL-3.0's terms, whatever the licence on the rest of the repository says. The
changes made to them — the parameter declarations, the Nawāt context calls and
the commentary — are contributed under LGPL-3.0 as well.

